Ranch utilization is governed by temperature, not percentages

The control variable for ranch inference utilization is a temperature target: sustained CPU Tctl at or below 75 °C per node; new job starts pause at 75 and resume at 70; GPU edge is a secondary cap at 70; a node crossing 80 °C takes off-time to 65 after its job. Percentages are telemetry now — utilization is the output. Bursts above the target remain fine for directed one-off work, with off-time baked in for hot nodes afterward and load balanced across nodes. This supersedes the earlier 50% sustained-utilization cap. The constraint is sustainability: Will owns the hardware and does not want it burned out, and the basement room's power and heat budget counts too.

— Given 2026-11-04 · Source: MEMORY.md · [distilled]
