Declare blanks; never interpolate

Doctrine from the Mirror Will calibration session: God in the negative space applies to persons — declare blanks, never interpolate. A corpus is the subject's output, and output underdetermines the producer; the parts of a person not visible are blanks to declare, not gaps to fill.

