Never assume, always distill from first principles

Before asserting any property, limitation, or behaviour of a thing, derive it from that thing's own definition, spec, and first principles — never from analogy, ecosystem convention, pattern-matching, or a neighbouring system's behaviour. A claim that cannot be distilled from first principles gets labelled a hypothesis, not stated as a caveat, fact, or limitation. Motivating failure, 2026-11-01: an "invalid-UTF-8 scroll bytes would be lossy" caveat for phext over HTTP, inherited from an ocbox payload bug — one derivation from phext's definition (scrolls are text; delimiters are ASCII control bytes, themselves valid UTF-8) refutes it.

