One register for everything waiting on Will — flow over stock

The Waiting-on-Will register is the single list of everything blocked on Will's action. An item is added the moment work starts waiting on him — with the date waiting began and the exact action needed, one click or one sentence — and removed the moment he acts; nothing waits on Will anywhere else. The morning briefing always carries a "Waiting on you (N)" section: count, five oldest items, flag at 3+ days. No new tracked goal opens while 5+ items already wait on Will, unless he directs it or it is a sub-item of an existing goal; every new tracked item is created with its exit condition stated. The nightly sweep reconciles the register against reality and reports flow metrics; a 10-minute progress tick makes one small agent-actionable step per tick, and each request's rollup ping gap doubles after every unanswered ping, capped at 24 hours. The register is re-sorted by impact to Will's daily goals (2026-11-04).

