Exception to the never-force-push rule, in Will's words: "whenever I ask for a rebase, I want it force pushed unless it impacts anyone except us." A Will-requested rebase is force-pushed with --force-with-lease, never bare --force, with the old history preserved on a backup branch first — unless the rewrite would impact anyone except us: other collaborators' work, open PRs it would strand, or external consumers of the history. Impact beyond us means stop at a branch push and report what was found.

