Links go at the end of the message, never with a question or options below them

Clicking a link in the chat app loses Will's state and scroll position below the link, so links go at the end of messages, never with a question or options below them — and anything Will needs to act on is re-sent in a following message after a link-bearing one.

— Given 2026-11-01 · Source: MEMORY.md · [distilled]
— Placed at 31.7.10/10.7.13/7.7.10 by holographic merge of the statement above: 15 distinct words — 15 placed from CYOA, 0 at home, 0 at the far corner.
Model phext stores as fine-grained per-field scrolls, never one JSON blob

Use phext itself as the database: fine-grained per-field, per-record scrolls addressed by coordinate, so an edit is a single small SQ update at one coordinate — hyper-fast and simple. Do not collapse a phext store into one JSON blob scroll, and do not reach for JSON structures where phext is the store.

