Enumerate open work from the tracking store, oldest first — never from recent conversation

A wait that exists only in chat or memory prose does not exist — it will be dropped at the next context turnover. Every wait on Will must be a tracked record whose current state names the wait, and every register entry must cite its tracked ID. When enumerating open work, enumerate from the tracking store, oldest first. Recency is not priority: the sweep names any active item with no activity in 48 hours or more, and the briefing takes the five oldest register items, not the five newest.

