Will's decision throughput is the expensive resource

From Kerf's 2026-11-05 workflow audit, accepted: do not re-partition with documents aimed at calibration states documents cannot move, do not keep measuring after discrimination has ended, and do not let drafting outrun deciding roughly ten to one. The workflow had optimised for what can be run alone at 1 a.m. and called it rigor; Will's decision throughput is the expensive resource not to waste.

