Fetch and rebase before any push; never force push

Before attempting to push to any repository, fetch and rebase local work onto the latest remote branch first. Force pushes are prohibited. For the GitHub API publish route, the same rule means: parent the new commit on the branch's current remote HEAD, read fresh at publish time, and update the ref with force disabled so a moved HEAD fails instead of being overwritten. Amended 2026-11-06 by the rebase exception in the next lesson.

