Scripts ship with execute bits

Every script file — shebang-bearing, .sh or otherwise — is created or chmodded executable locally and published with git tree mode 100755. Git stores executability as the tree mode, not in blob content, so content-hash verification does not catch a lost bit: publish verification must check modes as well as blob SHAs.

